#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example simulates a vehicle with a suspension lift kit. Most suspension lift kits work by lowering the wheel center height relative to the CG of the sprung mass.
#
#The sprung mass of the vehicle linked to this example, "Pickup, Full Size: Lifted (SA_SA)", is the same as the non-lifted full-size pickup truck, "Pickup, Full Size." The only difference is the wheel center heights on this truck are lower relative to the sprung mass coordinate system. Since the ground is defined as the bottom of the tires, this has the effect of lifting the sprung mass.
#
#This example also demonstrates how to create a road with a large smooth bump. Click on the Procedures blue link "Large Smooth Bump" for more information.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

